#: ../../source/references_scenes.md:5
msgid "Scene Design Philosophy"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_scenes.md:7
msgid "Scenes are storytelling units, not effect demos. Every scene needs:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_scenes.md:8
msgid ""
"A **concept** — what is happening visually? Not \"plasma + rings\" but "
"\"emergence from void\" or \"crystallization\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_scenes.md:9
msgid ""
"An **arc** — how does it change over its duration? Build, decay, "
"transform, reveal?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_scenes.md:10
msgid ""
"A **role** — how does it serve the larger video narrative? Opening "
"tension, peak energy, resolution?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_scenes.md:12
msgid ""
"The design patterns below provide compositional techniques. The scene "
"examples show them in practice at increasing complexity. The protocol "
"section covers the technical contract."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_scenes.md:14
msgid ""
"Good scene design starts with the concept, then selects effects and "
"parameters that serve it. The design patterns section shows *how* to "
"compose layers intentionally. The examples section shows complete working"
" scenes at every complexity level. The protocol section covers the "
"technical contract that all scenes must follow."
msgstr ""

